Global Map Japan, © Geospatial Information Authority of Japan

The .met metadata files inside the zips of versions 2.1 and 2.2, and the
Read_me.txt of the 2.1 transportation zip, still state an older condition
("Application procedure is required in using the product, except for
non-commercial purpose and use in small quantity. ..."). That condition is
outdated; the current terms are those above. The files are left in GSI's
zips unchanged.

The files under raw/<version>/ are GSI's own zips, byte for byte; each
version's MANIFEST.json records their URLs, sizes, sha256 and Last-Modified.

The Parquet under parquet/<version>/<layer>.parquet was made by
yuiseki/gsi-global-map-jp from the Shapefiles in the all-layers zip of each
vector version (2.0, 2.1, 2.2). This is an edited form of GSI's data, not a
GSI product, and GSI has not reviewed it:

  - each Shapefile became one GeoParquet 1.0.0 file, read with GDAL through
    DuckDB's spatial extension
  - columns were typed by name (the Global Map attribute codes and pop and
    ypc as integers); every other column is the text of the DBF, trimmed of
    surrounding spaces as GDAL reads it (one value, laa " Ogasawara Mura" in
    polbnda, loses a leading space)
  - a column fid was added: the record's position in the Shapefile, from 0
  - the M values of the PolyLineM layers (only 0 or the Shapefile no-data
    value) were dropped; x and y are unchanged
  - coordinates were not reprojected; each file states the CRS its .prj
    names (ITRF94, EPSG:8994, or JGD2000, EPSG:4612)
  - no other value was changed; the rasters were not converted

The code that fetches, checks and converts is in the repository this
dataset was built from (https://github.com/yuiseki/gsi-global-map-jp); its
licence does not apply here.
